WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Tomorrow’s calendar is full, but your day needs more than meetings.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.940
Dayweave connects Gmail, Google Calendar, and Google Sheets to make room for

3
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.340
rest, coffee, and lunch. This walkthrough uses sample data.

4
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.180
Start with sleep. Your morning commitments and the routines you choose shape

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.740
a suggested wake-up and wind-down time.

6
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.040
Open the explanation to see the calendar evidence and preferences behind it.

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.860
Next, coffee. Receipt purchase times suggest a familiar window, while your
calendar

8
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.740
helps find an opening. Dayweave keeps purchase history separate from what you

9
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.080
actually drank.

10
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.020
Gemini helps prioritize the plan using limited planning context.

11
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.780
The activity view shows its work, and scheduling checks keep suggested times

12
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.560
grounded in your calendar.

13
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.980
Then turn a suggestion into an action.

14
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.760
Choose lunch, review the exact event and activity entry, and confirm.

15
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.460
Repeat the approval, and Dayweave recognizes the existing reservation.

16
00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.680
There’s still just one activity record.

17
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.940
Nutrition is an optional feature within this day-planning workflow.

18
00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.320
Choose a food goal, and familiar receipt patterns suggest ideas for your

19
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.820
coffee break, lunch, or next grocery trip.

20
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.380
These are suggestions you can explore, not a diagnosis of your diet.

21
00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.960
For a longer view, the monthly calculator estimates one food using quantities

22
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.920
and sharing assumptions you enter.

23
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.860
It shows a conditional average, not your total intake.

24
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.780
From preparing for sleep to protecting a break, you decide what fits.

25
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.340
Dayweave brings the plan together, then acts only with your approval.

26
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.091
Google integrations were tested separately; wearable data is a future
connection.
